🎲🎲🎲 EXIT CODE: 0 🎲🎲🎲
🟩🟩🟩 STDOUT️ 🟩🟩🟩️
Request to change a domain's contact owner.<br/>
If you specify the `organization_id` of the domain's new owner, the contact will change from the current owner's Scaleway account to the new owner's Scaleway account.<br/>
If the new owner's current contact information is not available, the first ever contact they have created for previous domains is taken into account to operate the change.<br/>
If the new owner has never created a contact to register domains before, an error message displays.

USAGE:
  scw domain order trade [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  domain                                                                  The domain name to trade (change of owner/registrant).
  [project-id]                                                            Project ID to associate with the domain after the trade. Also used to filter the new owner's contacts.
  [new-owner-contact-id]                                                  ID of the existing contact to use as the domain's new owner.
  [new-owner-contact.legal-form]                                          Legal form of the contact (individual, corporate, association, other). (legal_form_unknown | individual | corporate | association | other)
  [new-owner-contact.firstname]                                           First name of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.lastname]                                            Last name of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.company-name]                                        Company name of the contact (required for corporate legal forms).
  [new-owner-contact.email]                                               Email address of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.email-alt]                                           Alternative email address of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.phone-number]                                        Phone number of the contact, normalized to +CC.NationalNumber format.
  [new-owner-contact.fax-number]                                          Fax number of the contact, normalized to +CC.NationalNumber format.
  [new-owner-contact.address-line-1]                                      First line of the contact's address.
  [new-owner-contact.address-line-2]                                      Second line of the contact's address.
  [new-owner-contact.zip]                                                 Postal code of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.city]                                                City of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.country]                                             Country code of the contact (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 format).
  [new-owner-contact.vat-identification-code]                             VAT identification code of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.company-identification-code]                         Company identification code of the contact (SIRET/SIREN for French contacts, any format for others).
  [new-owner-contact.lang]                                                Preferred language of the contact. (unknown_language_code | en_US | fr_FR | de_DE)
  [new-owner-contact.resale]                                              Indicates whether the contact's information can be resold.
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.mode]                                    (mode_unknown | individual | company_identification_code | duns | local | association | trademark | code_auth_afnic)
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.individual-info.whois-opt-in]           
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.duns-info.duns-id]                      
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.duns-info.local-id]                     
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.association-info.publication-jo]        
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.association-info.publication-jo-page]   
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.trademark-info.trademark-inpi]          
  [new-owner-contact.extension-fr.code-auth-afnic-info.code-auth-afnic]   
  [new-owner-contact.extension-eu.european-citizenship]                   
  [new-owner-contact.whois-opt-in]                                        Indicates whether the contact's information is published in the WHOIS database.
  [new-owner-contact.state]                                               State or region of the contact.
  [new-owner-contact.extension-nl.legal-form]                              (legal_form_unknown | other | non_dutch_eu_company | non_dutch_legal_form_enterprise_subsidiary | limited_company | limited_company_in_formation | cooperative | limited_partnership | sole_company | european_economic_interest_group | religious_entity | partnership | public_company | mutual_benefit_company | residential | shipping_company | foundation | association | trading_partnership | natural_person)
  [new-owner-contact.extension-nl.legal-form-registration-number]         
  [new-owner-contact.extension-it.pin]                                    Domain name registrant's Taxcode (mandatory / only optional when the trustee is used)
  [new-owner-contact.questions.{index}.question]                          
  [new-owner-contact.questions.{index}.answer]                            

DEPRECATED ARGS:
  [new-owner-contact.extension-it.european-citizenship]   This option is useless anymore
  [new-owner-contact.extension-it.tax-code]               Tax_code is renamed to pin

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for trade
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
